(2485216, 339083, 37893, '<td valign="top">This one is a bit washed out IMHO. The colors are there but just needs to be bumped just a tad for them to show up. The mis-aligned horizontals are a no-no in Architecture shots. The interest is there with the details but the window reflections do not in any way enhance the image. If there''s a way that you can use a polarizer then by all means, do so. They take out reflections pretty well. There is some sort of barrel distortion happening to the image as seen in the horizontals which is also distracting. The use of three windows is good as most odd assymetrical compositions works well. The lights could have been cloned out as well since this was an advanced editing challenge.</td>', 'This one is a bit washed out IMHO. The colors are there but just needs to be bumped just a tad for them to show up. The mis-aligned horizontals are a no-no in Architecture shots. The interest is there with the details but the window reflections do not in any way enhance the image. If there''s a way that you can use a polarizer then by all means, do so. They take out reflections pretty well. There is some sort of barrel distortion happening to the image as seen in the horizontals which is also distracting. The use of three windows is good as most odd assymetrical compositions works well. The lights could have been cloned out as well since this was an advanced editing challenge.', '2006-06-05 02:25:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2485224, 339124, 58047, '<td valign="top">I prefer the thumbnail view to the full size version of this shot, the thumbnail view to me resembles a cartoon fairytale, but the illusion doesn''t hold up with the larger shot, however the reflections do add character to the bridge. Congrats on your ribbon.</td>', 'I prefer the thumbnail view to the full size version of this shot, the thumbnail view to me resembles a cartoon fairytale, but the illusion doesn''t hold up with the larger shot, however the reflections do add character to the bridge. Congrats on your ribbon.', '2006-06-05 02:27:20.000000', NULL, 0),
