(2485306, 339211, 27735, '<td valign="top">Yep, used a polarizer to get the very dark sky. Other than that, just converted to b/w and did the usual resize and sharpen.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by adine:</b></div><hr/><i> Good work with bright light - nice tonal range from dark to light. Must have used a polarlizer too?  Great dark sky.  Nice composition with the 90 degree angle at the bottom contrasting with the soaring curve of the dome. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Yep, used a polarizer to get the very dark sky. Other than that, just converted to b/w and did the usual resize and sharpen. Originally posted by adine: Good work with bright light - nice tonal range from dark to light. Must have used a polarlizer too?  Great dark sky.  Nice composition with the 90 degree angle at the bottom contrasting with the soaring curve of the dome. ', '2006-06-05 02:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
