(2486099, 339608, 7628, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TheMegalomaniac:</b></div><hr/><i> I also made the mistake of waiting for dusk because I hoped the lighting would be more interesting then. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You know those pictures you took do have excellent colors - I don''t think dusk was a mistake.  Maybe bring a tripod next time and go for a longer exposure.  The reflective nature of the buliding makes it ideal to photograph in different light conditions (Monet would have had a GREAT time with this!)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by TheMegalomaniac: I also made the mistake of waiting for dusk because I hoped the lighting would be more interesting then.   You know those pictures you took do have excellent colors - I don''t think dusk was a mistake.  Maybe bring a tripod next time and go for a longer exposure.  The reflective nature of the buliding makes it ideal to photograph in different light conditions (Monet would have had a GREAT time with this!) ', '2006-06-05 09:53:14.000000', NULL, 0),
